<title>UK: Tesco aims to buy Wigan ground, sponsor club.</title>
<headline>Tesco aims to buy Wigan ground, sponsor club.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>British supermarket group Tesco Plc intends to sponsor Wigan Rugby League Football Club as it moves to buy the club's Central Park ground for 12 million stg.</p>
<p>A statement from the company said it would become a &quot;principal sponsor&quot; of Wigan, situated in northern England, along with electricity company Norweb and Nike sportswear.</p>
<p>Tesco is in the process of exchanging contracts to buy Central Park, a spokesman said, and would intend to build a new supermarket on the site.</p>
<p>Central Park has been home to Wigan since 1902 and the club may use the ground of Bolton Wanderers on a temporary basis, newspaper reports said.</p>
<p>Tesco said the sponsorship deal would be worth &quot;several million pounds.&quot;</p>
